   "text": "WILLIAM MERVIN MILLS\n24\nAthletics\nClass of 1984\nDate of birth: June 30, 1938\nBirthplace: Pine Ridge, SD\nHometown: Fair Oaks, CA\nCollege: University of Kansas\nDuring the 1964 Tokyo Olympic Games he became the\nfirst American to win the 10,000 meters as a virtual\nunknown, setting an Olympic record in the process. Mills\nalso set a world record in the six-mile run during the AAU\nchampionships in 1965. Part Sioux Indian, Mills became\nactive with Indian affairs and, subsequently, a movie of his\nlife, \"Running Brave,\" was made in 1983. In 1964 he had\nserved as a First Lieutenant in the U.S. Marine Corps and\nlater became an insurance sales agent. Mills is currently\npresident of Billy Mills Enterprises.\nCareer Highlights:\n1964 Tokyo Olympic Games\n10,000 meters\nGold medal*\n• Olympic record",
